{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless","id":36324,"title":"Tell me about your Nameless","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-24T06:07:31-08:00","id":36324,"title":"Tell me about your Nameless","content":"Seriously, the Nameless is one of the coolest things in B&amp;S in my opinion (I mean, he feels like Requiem version of the Emissary of Nexus from Exalted) and after I've made thousands of theories about VII and the strixs, now my brain can't stop thinking about what the Nameless could be.. Because of his aesthetics (shadowy figure with glowing eyes) and his seemingly dislike toward Lancea et Sanctum, I think it is connected to the strixs somehow- so here are few theories my mind made up for him:<br /> <br /> a) an evolved strix. When strixs lives long enough and manage not to split itself, it start absorbing other strixs until it turns into an human like form.<br /> <br /> b) The Nameless is to the Man what the strixs are to the Beast, hence his control over Theban Sorcery. He is also just the first one- and there are others in the way.<br /> <br /> c) Remember that it was said that if a strix use Synthesis over a supernatural being, weird things happen? This is what happen when it use it on a demon. It stopped the Theban Sorcery for seeing it as part of the God Machine's influence, and limits the number of kindred to 4 because for demons 4 is really a magical number.<br /> <br /> so, what about your theories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T08:52:54-08:00","id":36399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless#post36324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c) Remember that it was said that if a strix use Synthesis over a supernatural being, weird things happen? This is what happen when it use it on a demon. It stopped the Theban Sorcery for seeing it as part of the God Machine's influence, and limits the number of kindred to 4 because for demons 4 is really a magical number.<br /> <br /> so, what about your theories?</div> </div> </div> </div>This thought came to mind when I read it as well. I didn't go demon though, like Bloody Mary (which I intend to use in such a fashion) from Danse Macabre I felt it had a feel of True Fae/Strix (well I didn't think Strix then like I do now). I hope as other updated core books come down the line that the lines blur some more so that the world feels organically together. Nothing blunt, just hints of possibilities that can be picked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T17:10:20-08:00","id":37074,"title":"","content":"I didnt see the nameless in the book, yet, but it sounds like a Shadow Person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1751-blackrajanya","name":"BlackRajanya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T17:29:39-08:00","id":37080,"title":"","content":"It's some kind of existing boogey man in the short description of Montreal. &quot;It&quot; is responsible for the Kindred not playing &quot;the Grand Game&quot;. It is blamed for the death of two dozen Kindred in a single event in 1970, preventing a &quot;hostile political takeover&quot;. It set up rules that all Kindred follow since then...<br /> Sounds like great story potential!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#A52A2A\">Am I man<br /> or am I beast<br /> or am I just like you?</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1701-ags","name":"AGS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:24:58-08:00","id":75911,"title":"","content":"Thread necromancy: I don't know if this has been brought up before: Tsihstekeri, the Ventrue line in the city, means &quot;owl&quot; in Mohawk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T03:59:22-08:00","id":76180,"title":"","content":"Hm - fun fact in Nigeria and parts of West Africa it's desperately bad luck to call an owl by its name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:34:09-08:00","id":76232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76180#post76180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm - fun fact in Nigeria and parts of West Africa it's desperately bad luck to call an owl by its name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very bad luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T08:55:29-08:00","id":76311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76232#post76232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very, very bad luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally you refer to them as 'the bird that scares you' or 'those evil birds'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:50:00-08:00","id":76662,"title":"","content":"Creepy Fact: I know a senior citizen that keeps an owl skull in a bag above her front door to keep evil spirits out. Apparently the spirit of the owl scares away the nasty things. (Makes you wonder how mean the owl spirit has to be in order to do that, right?)<br /> Folklore is nice sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:08:42-08:00","id":76674,"title":"","content":"I assumed it was just a powerful Gangrel with full mastery of protean. I can't remember the name but the 5 dot power for protean lets you transform into a smoke cloud with glowing eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:12:36-08:00","id":76678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76232#post76232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very, very bad luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all thread was worth it just to see that comment :P<br /> <br /> However- I've just thought about something: because of the aesthetics of the Nameless and the fact that B&amp;S present the strixs as &quot;story triggers&quot;, it kinda makes the connection between the Nameless and the Owls into almost too obvious.. so wouldn't it be scarier if the Nameless wouldn't be connected to the strixs? I mean, here come the characters, who did an extensive research about the strixs, and who are sure that they finally ready to get rid of the mysterious tyrant of Montreal- when they discover that they made a big (maybe even fatal) mistake...<br /> <br /> any ideas about that line of thought?<br /> <br /> (edit- not that I have any problem with connecting the Nameless to the strixs. I really like thinking that there is a connection- but I simply wonder about any other possibilities)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T16:34:41-08:00","id":76690,"title":"","content":"I know nothing about mages. And neither do vampires. A mage with a hair up his arse about kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:16:11-08:00","id":76713,"title":"","content":"I honestly considered that it may be one of the Gentry, personally. Some funky one that has some Shadow People (as previously mused) like Themes, or one of those entities from the Death Dream dominion from Book of the Dead if it wasn't a Strix. Seemed an interesting alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:46:04-08:00","id":76737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76678#post76678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This all thread was worth it just to see that comment :P<br /> <br /> However- I've just thought about something: because of the aesthetics of the Nameless and the fact that B&amp;S present the strixs as &quot;story triggers&quot;, it kinda makes the connection between the Nameless and the Owls into almost too obvious.. so wouldn't it be scarier if the Nameless wouldn't be connected to the strixs? I mean, here come the characters, who did an extensive research about the strixs, and who are sure that they finally ready to get rid of the mysterious tyrant of Montreal- when they discover that they made a big (maybe even fatal) mistake...<br /> <br /> any ideas about that line of thought?<br /> <br /> (edit- not that I have any problem with connecting the Nameless to the strixs. I really like thinking that there is a connection- but I simply wonder about any other possibilities)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason it seems too obvious. There are some clues people haven't picked up on yet (at least, nobody's posted about on the forums). A couple of the clues have come up. But not the ones I'd call essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:22:45-08:00","id":76755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76737#post76737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a reason it seems too obvious. There are some clues people haven't picked up on yet (at least, nobody's posted about on the forums). A couple of the clues have come up. But not the ones I'd call essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Rule V and the unstated headcount cutoff in Rule II among those clues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-21-2014, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T23:09:30-08:00","id":76884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76755#post76755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Rule V and the unstated headcount cutoff in Rule II among those clues?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are very important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T00:23:53-08:00","id":76897,"title":"","content":"Rule 2's focus on the number four has a very Demon feel to it. And taken as a whole there's a very infrastructure and occult matrix vibe going on. Is the Nameless an Angel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T03:33:05-08:00","id":76959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76737#post76737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason it seems too obvious. There are some clues people haven't picked up on yet (at least, nobody's posted about on the forums). A couple of the clues have come up. But not the ones I'd call essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the Pit of the Nameless. But somehow I am not feeling comfortable using an entity that I as the storyteller don't understand. So far it looks like whoever the nameless is, he is appearing to guard Montreal from the Strix - except I think he isn't. Is he Kindred, Strix or something else? I've got to read the entry again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:01:08-08:00","id":76964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76959#post76959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But somehow I am not feeling comfortable using an entity that I as the storyteller don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just use your own answer for your games. No need for guesswork or doing what others do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:36:03-08:00","id":76974,"title":"","content":"Yes that's what I am going to do, if I use this set-up. But I am still looking for an answer that will be hard to guess by the players and also surprise them.<br /> <br /> Just noticing: If only four or fewer Kindred are allowed to gather, it will never be possible to get a representative of each Covenant or Clan to a meeting of kindred spirits. Thus, neither the Clans nor the Covenants will be able to fully ally against the Nameless. At most, four of those entities might be able to conspire at a time, never the whole population. Always leaving one clan or covenant out cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:38:47-08:00","id":76975,"title":"","content":"Rules 2 and 3 imply a quarantine to me: don't bunch together, and don't leave the city. Rules 1 and 5 keep chaos down; no murdering each other, and no stirring up panic by impersonating the Nameless. These four rules, along with the removal of Theban Sorcery, largely hamstring Kindred society; no large gatherings, no threats of execution to keep the masses following a leader, and half the magic is gone. All this paints the Nameless as working some sort of weird social experiment with the Kindred of Montreal, one aimed at (to use some meta terminology) ensuring nobody goes beyond Tier 1 and instead has to rely ln themself and a small coterie at best. It empowers the individual and the small group by making anything that enforces a social hierarchy nearly impossible. Rules 4 and 6 don't fit into my theory at all, of course, and neither does the lack of a ban on Cru\u00e1c or whatever the Tsihsketeri know. Rule 6 confuses me more than anything; what does a church cross have to do with any readily-apparent theory? No ready tie to the Strix, the dismembering of the social establishment, or any sort of ancient native prophecy pop out to me at all. As for what the hell the Nameless is, I'm just as lost as anyone else and clearly must write it off as the demon from Montreal By Night hopping from oWoD to nWoD somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:49:59-08:00","id":76978,"title":"","content":"well, from what I can gather from the Rules, I think that there are a number of conclusions:<br /> <br /> a) The Nameless need vampires. Sure, it doesn't allow them to do big gatherings and kills them every time they break the Rules, but it needs them. Rules I to III show it. So what ever the Nameless is, and how powerful it may be, it needs the kindred, and it invest so much energy and resources in order to keep them in line because it is THAT important.<br /> <br /> b) Rule IV seems to be kinda obvious- but this IS rule IV, and 4 is the magic number, so I believe that there is something beneath the surface.. I believe that that Rule is the most important one, and that it exist for the same reason Rule V exist- in order to keep the Nameless nameless. For some reason, like it needs vampires, it also needs to keep itself as a mystery. That make me think that maybe the Nameless gains something from being the only terror in the night- and if someone tries to impersonate it, he may hurt the complicate plan of the Nameless.<br /> <br /> c) The last Rule seems to be the weirdest of all the others- all of the Rules exist, more or less, on the personal level. Suddenly, there is a Rule that targets a specific thing- the Cross. The reason seems to be connected to the fact that the Cross is the trigger to this all plan- this is where the first Prince was killed, and by doing so Theban Sorcery stopped working. To me, it sounds like it was some of a ceremony- killing a &quot;Prince&quot; upon a &quot;Royal Cross&quot;. In short, if one wants to allow Theban Sorcery to work again, or to destroy the complicate plan of the Nameless, it should involve the Mount Royal Cross.<br /> <br /> Now, if we add that to the fact that those who know the most are a line of vampires which is named after Owls (which we don't need the native American mythology from Wikipedia to tell us that they are a bad sign) and that they claim that the Nameless is the least among their problems and that there are worse things in the way... well, I don't have a clue about what comes out, but it reeks I tell you!<br /> <br /> Edit- yeah, I've had a sudden relaization that the &quot;Cross&quot; may not actually mean the Church, but the Royal Mount Cross, for this was were everything has started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-22-2014, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:55:03-08:00","id":76982,"title":"","content":"(Apologies for the double post: these forums do not get along well with an iPad.) I've found a minor break in the case! The Rue Saint Paul (a street in the city) is said to be haunted, and Kindred who lurk there meet ill fates. According to the Great and All-Knowing Wikipedia, Rue Saint Paul is the oldest street in Montreal, and was originally laid out by Fran\u00e7ois Dollier de Casson, a chaplain who served the French soldiers who fought against the local Mohawk in an action that may well be the one that led to the French Kindred's &quot;ghoul farm&quot; of natives.<br /> <br /> Given that the natives don't fear the Nameless, that it made its first attack at the Cross, has a Rule against approaching the Cross, removed the magic practiced by Christian Kindred from Montreal, and haunts a street plotted by a chaplain involved in an atrocity against the natives, you start to get a picture of the Nameless as something somewhat on the side of the Tsihsketeri and violently opposed to Christianity. Not sure how this ties into Kindred at large, but nobody else mentioned it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-23-2014, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:11:38-08:00","id":77045,"title":"","content":"Wait, have we done this topic before? I may be completely wrong in my remembering, but this seems spookily similar to another topic a little while ago. Some of these responses are giving off very palatable senses of deja vu O.O<br /> <br /> But back to the topic at hand, for our group while I have not done a Blood and Smoke game yet (though it's on the table), I have been toying around with what/who the Nameless may be. Due to the sudden inability to use ANY Theban Sorcery in Montreal, I have made the assumption that perhaps that the Nameless is actually Vahishtael, the very entity that revealed the secrets of Theban Sorcery to Saint Daniel. So to answer this question, I imagine ( for our setting at least) the Nameless to indeed be an Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:46:45-08:00","id":77095,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought about the Rue Saint Paul. But it clearly inleague with the Tsihsketeri. I really doubt its something other than a strix or a vampire.<br /> <br /> My guess is that he is the Tsihsketeri prince of the city, probably their founder risen from torpor. Think about it. he has the pwer to set and enforce rules, and there are no other power structures in town. Being ancient, he is powerful and has great knowledge of cruac, being able to desacrate the cross as part of a ritual to disrupt theban sorcery. and maybe even take control of a strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T17:24:53-08:00","id":77416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76978#post76978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit- yeah, I've had a sudden relaization that the &quot;Cross&quot; may not actually mean the Church, but the Royal Mount Cross, for this was were everything has started.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the Cross literally meant the Royal Mount Cross. It now occurs to me that it could be a poetic reference to the church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T02:09:19-08:00","id":77545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77045#post77045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But back to the topic at hand, for our group while I have not done a Blood and Smoke game yet (though it's on the table), I have been toying around with what/who the Nameless may be. Due to the sudden inability to use ANY Theban Sorcery in Montreal, I have made the assumption that perhaps that the Nameless is actually Vahishtael, the very entity that revealed the secrets of Theban Sorcery to Saint Daniel. So to answer this question, I imagine ( for our setting at least) the Nameless to indeed be an Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, It strikes me that the Nameless is related to the church in some way due to having the ability to prevent Theban Sorcery from happening and with such a large area to supress, it would have to be a tier 4 entity and there are only a handful of those named in VtR.<br /> <br /> Knowledge of Sorcery, tier 4 entity, killed someone at a cross...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 02-23-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T05:56:09-08:00","id":77610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77545#post77545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowledge of Sorcery, tier 4 entity, killed someone at a cross...</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by &quot;tier 4 entity&quot;? What is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:51:41-08:00","id":77651,"title":"","content":"If Tier 3 is global. Tier 4 might be cosmic?!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T08:11:12-08:00","id":77654,"title":"","content":"I must say that I don't think that the Nameless is a Tsihsketeri seek for vengeance. The reason is that the Tsihsketeri don't believe they shouldn't fear it because it is their friend, but because its existence means that there are worse things in the horizon.<br /> <br /> Also, it occurred to me that whether the Nameless is a vampire, a strixs or something else, it doesn't really understand the modern Kindred. After all, it didn't gave them the rules right at the beginning, but too its time, spreading terror until it finally gave out the rules. While spreading terror may be its purpose, I'm not sure it is- after all, at the beginning it killed a prince after a prince until he gave a specific message for &quot;no more princes&quot;, so I think that there is a certain ignorance from its side about how vampire works.<br /> <br /> so it made me think about two different possibilities:<br /> <br /> a) the Nameless seek chaos. Everything it does is done in order to make things more and more crazy. It needs the vampires for some reason (like the fact that it killed the prince on the Cross in order to stop Theban Sorcery), but it doesn't want them to interfere with its project. Its greatest secret is that there is no real higher meaning for the Rules- they are simply made in order to draw of attention from its project, which involves Theban Sorcery and vampires. In a way, it was like giving the Kindred a riddle to solve which had no solution so they would leave it alone.<br /> <br /> b) the Nameless is a defense mechanism against something bad- really bad. It has existed since the times the Tsihsketeri ruled the land, and so they know what it truly means. All of those weird Rules are a some kind of a ritual meant to protect the vampires of Montreal, and if it would fail what ever the Nameless tries to stop will be free to kill everything. The thing may be based around the vampiric Beast (so the chances are that it is connected to the strixs), which is why it drain the very energy of Theban Sorcery in order to create some kind of a barrier or a seal upon it. The very presence of vampires is needed in order to work the ritual because of the Vitae in their vines which carries mystical energy<br /> <br /> c) same as before- only that instead of stopping some great evil, it tried to summon it. Maybe it even tries to awake God himself- and from what I remember from Danse Macabre, it truly isn't a good thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:58:03-08:00","id":77936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77610#post77610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by &quot;tier 4 entity&quot;? What is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tier 4 is the cosmic level. It's where Archmages, Spirits such as Luna and Gaia, Death Lords, The Judges of Daut, and more operate.<br /> <br /> In VtR, an example would be the Crone, Vahishtael, Beilial, Longinus, Dracula, and the odd number of methuselahs that are still roaming around.<br /> <br /> In order to shut down the ability to use Theban sorcery, The nameless would have to be at this level of play.<br /> <br /> Of course that begs the question: did the Nameless use Cr\u00faac or Theban sorcery to lock down the area? Killing a Prince for a ritual would satisfy a ritual for both of the styles...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:48:01-08:00","id":77966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77936#post77936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tier 4 is the cosmic level. It's where Archmages, Spirits such as Luna and Gaia, Death Lords, The Judges of Daut, and more operate.<br /> <br /> In VtR, an example would be the Crone, Vahishtael, Beilial, Longinus, Dracula, and the odd number of methuselahs that are still roaming around.<br /> <br /> In order to shut down the ability to use Theban sorcery, The nameless would have to be at this level of play.<br /> <br /> Of course that begs the question: did the Nameless use Cr\u00faac or Theban sorcery to lock down the area? Killing a Prince for a ritual would satisfy a ritual for both of the styles...</div> </div> </div> </div>What if he doesn't sing either of those songs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:59:08-08:00","id":77971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77966#post77966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if he doesn't sing either of those songs?</div> </div> </div> </div>...a Threnody?<br /> <br /> (I'm going to smack myself for not getting this when someone does clue in. Mark my words.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T19:01:52-08:00","id":77973,"title":"","content":"One of the great things about the World of Darkness is the unstated danger of knowledge. We feel at our most vulnerable when we are ignorant, and thus we seek to grow in knowledge, boxing and categorizing everything into concepts and conceits we understand and can deal with. And because we feel we know these things, we try to make as much of the world fit under those concepts until we gain enough knowledge to break it into another category.<br /> <br /> The danger, then, is that we are prone to thinking of any unknown as one thing when it is very probably an other.<br /> <br /> No, that's not a typo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T21:46:47-08:00","id":78076,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Nameless is just a (or many) clever vampire.<br /> <br /> - The name of the Ventrue Prince, Thomas Sheridan, is shared with an irish actor who is known for his work on elocution (how you behave on stage). That guy specialized on how to deliver messages and convince an audience of what you wanted them to believe.<br /> <br /> - The date of the Ventrue Prince's death, November 5th. And nobody went &quot;<i>Remember, remember... the 5th of November...</i>&quot;? Someone kills the figure of authority on the anniversary of an failed plot to topple a government. Someone has a sense for theatrics...<br /> <br /> - A young <i>unnamed </i>Carthian was the only witness to the Prince's demise which, honestly, reads like a well rehearsed play. <br /> <br /> - That night was named &quot;The Martyrdom&quot;. The name irks me. Martyr implies &quot;somebody who suffers persecution and death for advocating, refusing to renounce, and/or refusing to advocate a belief or cause, usually a religious one&quot;. The Prince was Invictus. Maybe he believed in some religion, but the term would have been better used for the Circle or the Lancea, The again, Thomas Sheridan's father, also named Thomas Sheridan, was an Anglican divine. I don't know...<br /> <br /> - The second execution has the same vibe as the first one. An <i>unnamed </i>neonate walks in by chance to be the only witness to the Seneschal's execution. I think a repeat of the Ventrue Prince's death was only to make a point.<br /> <br /> - Then, the Carthian Movement had a big party who was crashed by our Nameless. Everyone died with but one witness. There's always one witness to spread the word...<br /> <br /> - The only surviving Kindred had her eyes taken and won't regrow them. Maybe she was dominated... maybe she sincerely fears the Nameless... maybe she has glowing eyes... or maybe she's the damn Nameless... who knows!<br /> <br /> - The rules... the Nameless seems to have a keen awareness of every infraction. I call either Carthian Law, powerful blood sorcery or, like it was suggested, a threnody with either something like Lord of the Land (which coincidentally increases dread on its domain) or Auspex and the sacrifice may have been the Ventrue Prince to make the effects encompass the entirety of its domain (the whole island). With the last option, maybe the lost of theban sorcery is merely a side effect of the Beast's manifestation in the threnody.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Nameless is an icon. It never speaks (it is only rumored to). The only description is &quot;a black figure with shining eyes&quot;. The only one who saw the Nameless are outsiders and &quot;witnesses&quot; of those three nights. Very reliable sources...<br /> <br /> The state of the city in the Movement's paragraph: &quot;city without Elysiums, without formal feeding grounds, without proper law enforcement, and without all the trappings of a typical city&quot;. The rules stuck in stasis every Kindred take for granted don't apply. If this isn't a revolution where the established order and its traditions were toppled...<br /> <br /> Maybe the whole thing was a Carthian scheme to take the city. The goal of that Carthian reunion <i>was </i>to establish dominion. That night is called &quot;The End and the Beginning&quot;. Why? Technically, the Nameless has taken over since the death of the Invictus Prince. Isn't that the moment &quot;the End&quot; of the domain as they knew it? Or the Carthian reunion was the end of the construction of the icon that is the Nameless and the official beginning of their dominion? In a city where everyone operates in little cells, communication is everything and the Movement seems to control it with its communication network, phone trees and PO5170.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Nameless is simply a myth the Movement constructed to establish and maintain their leadership, one that the Kindred population is now too afraid of to even question or contest.<br /> <br /> Maybe the only reason the Tsihstekeri are exempt is because they are neutral, make an effort to stay on the sideline and have a truce with the Nameless. And that's why they know and the Ventrue who are told the secret don't fear the Nameless anymore because he isn't some boogeyman, but just another vampire.<br /> <br /> Why do those in the know are afraid of something else entirely? What is worse than a vampire is a vampire's predator. If you think the Nameless' rule is harsh, wait until the Strixes are unleashed! A whole population of encroached French Kindred were destroyed overnight by the natives after decades of being miserably on the losing end of the war. You need something <i>really </i>powerful the French never saw coming and it must have been an unconventional tactics as most conventional ones would have been used during those five decades and failed. Maybe Rue St-Paul is &quot;haunted&quot; because it is one of the oldest road of the city where one of the blood farms may have been and it still suffers from the fallout from those owls.<br /> <br /> One of the many possibilities. Maybe the Nameless is instead an old Nosferatu delighted by the fear induced by his rule while recreating the blood farms of the French, but with a vampire population so he can feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When in doubt... ... ... Everyone's grudge!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2362-mr-iki-iki","name":"Mr Iki Iki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T22:33:12-08:00","id":78095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77971#post77971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...a Threnody?<br /> <br /> (I'm going to smack myself for not getting this when someone does clue in. Mark my words.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring those, I would say a Threnody.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=77973#post77973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the great things about the World of Darkness is the unstated danger of knowledge. We feel at our most vulnerable when we are ignorant, and thus we seek to grow in knowledge, boxing and categorizing everything into concepts and conceits we understand and can deal with. And because we feel we know these things, we try to make as much of the world fit under those concepts until we gain enough knowledge to break it into another category.<br /> <br /> The danger, then, is that we are prone to thinking of any unknown as one thing when it is very probably an other.<br /> <br /> No, that's not a typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so. If anything, it's an exercise for the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 02-24-2014, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T05:08:10-08:00","id":78226,"title":"","content":"There are six rules. Where is the seventh? Or, dare I say it, rule number VII?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T05:59:22-08:00","id":78249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=78226#post78226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are six rules. Where is the seventh? Or, dare I say it, rule number VII?</div> </div> </div> </div>The seventh rule doesn't translate to text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T17:29:33-08:00","id":78834,"title":"","content":"Isn't rule number 7 or 0: No more princes? By the way, would the Carthian Law merits apply to the rules of the nameless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T19:53:47-08:00","id":79009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=78834#post78834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't rule number 7 or 0: No more princes? By the way, would the Carthian Law merits apply to the rules of the nameless?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they definitely would. They are recognized law in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:27:27-08:00","id":79461,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel like my joke about the Nameless being VII flew over a few heads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:08:22-08:00","id":79680,"title":"","content":"Well- it is because that while I recognized it was a joke, some part in my mind has started to think that there may be some logic in it....:P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T13:03:03-08:00","id":81745,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking back to Belial's Brood, the Nameless faction of the Hexad and certain city references scattered through the covenant book where Belial's Brood is strong. Also the angle Rose mentioned some time back regarding what a Brood Domain would look like, and if memory serves rather lawless, chaotic or otherwise indulgent. That could well be fine and well for the Brood, but how does one mitigate the other Covenants and Unbound from sytming what they want? No Prince, no large gatherings, don't look, don't impersonate, don't mess with the cross... Theban Sorcery going right out the window. Demiurge ascendant and &quot;there is no VII rule&quot;. Take that last notion as literally and it turns from &quot;It's the VII&quot; and instead points to &quot;They don't rule here, fear us&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just a few ways to spin it further. Liberally dash with with other Brood faction references (like the Pandemonium) for shits and giggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T13:37:52-08:00","id":82279,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of the Pawn and the Phantom from Damnation City. There is an image of Kindred Cant connected to the pawn, it's description in DC, p. 68 is: &quot;A crew of shadowy watchers/spies&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T23:46:41-07:00","id":100628,"title":"","content":"Potential idea (and a handy bit of thread necromancy): perhaps the Tsihsketeri aren't afraid of the Nameless because the Strix are riding all of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:32:36-08:00","id":365956,"title":"","content":"Might this be relevant to the apparent place of the Cross as some sort of lynchpin and the Nameless as a herald of something worse, or the possibility of its presence holding something back?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1643 a flood threatened the city. Maisonneuve prayed to the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virgin_Mary\" target=\"_blank\">Virgin Mary</a> to stop the inundation and when it abated, he erected a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Royal_Cross\" target=\"_blank\">cross</a> atop <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Royal\" target=\"_blank\">Mount Royal</a>. A cross has been maintained there to the current day. </div> </div> </div>And I just realized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1970 \u2013 St. Ann's Church (Griffintown) is torn down. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once, a coterie of Lancea et Sanctum broke the second rule and held a church gathering. No witnesses survived; the building burned with no escapes. </div> </div> </div>Was this where the Lancea held their gathering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-10-2015, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T22:25:55-08:00","id":366071,"title":"","content":"FWIW, my chapter of Secrets of the Covenants has some more information on Montreal. I don't know if anyone will catch it. But it's totally in there. Even though I think the spoiler is pretty blunt, I think it's more important what it says about the Movement. I figure people will get the wrong idea. But that's kind of the point of some mystery, isn't it?<br /> <br /> And yes. I was alluding to St. Ann's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 01-11-2015, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T14:35:06-08:00","id":366648,"title":"","content":"This is why I haven't touched the Pit of the Nameless since I first read the book, until someone (un)fortunately reminded me it existed.<br /> <br /> It didn't feel like every other story hook provided where the ST is the one who decides how things really are or has the freedom to chose the actual truth behind events. I could tell there was a story there, I could tell that it was written with something in mind, and I could tell that there was an actual truth there. I don't feel comfortable using the setting when all that's going on in the background but so close to any characters within is completely obscured like that. I wouldn't feel comfortable making my own interpretation or deciding the truth in my version because it would be like falsifying it. I wouldn't be able to invest myself in doing whatever I want with it, because I'm too invested in wanting to <b>really know what's going on.</b><br /> <br /> It understand it may sound like going against the spirit of the World Of Darkness. But this isn't a &quot;setting mystery&quot; like the origin of the Strix, or the Supernal War and the Lie, or the death of Father Wolf, or the truth of Irem and the Rite Of Return. This is something exclusive to Montreal, and <i>extremely personal</i> to every Kindred who lives there.<br /> <br /> I can't bring myself to care about creating subjective explanations to the Pit of the Nameless, when I know there's an objective one that is simply hidden from us. It's this close to the characters of the setting, so it doesn't open me to following speculations or accepting the distant vagueness as it is. It just makes me anxiously tear my hairs out at trying to understand it and frustrated that we're given so little to go on.<br /> <br /> The Pit of the Nameless isn't just a setting or a story hook to me. It's closer to a sinfully incomplete chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-11-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T14:50:22-08:00","id":366663,"title":"","content":"I get what you're saying but I find it interesting how two people can look at the same thing, this city, see the same thing, that there is a hard-set idea behind it, and come to completely different conclusions from that. I see absolutely no problem taking whatever set answer they have for Montreal or the Nameless, or really anything, and changing it to fit my stories.<br /> <br /> I would probably never use it as is anyways, because it's in Canada, but I'd find it easy to just take it, change some names, and put it pretty much anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T14:58:22-08:00","id":366672,"title":"","content":"Things that make you think often tend to lead to more than one conclusion, so that's only natural. I don't particularly need people to agree with me, and I can respect having a different opinion. I just wanted to explain my stance while we were at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-11-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:16:50-08:00","id":366706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=366648#post366648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't bring myself to care about creating subjective explanations to the Pit of the Nameless, when I know there's an objective one that is simply hidden from us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it helps you in any way, but there's not an objective truth. Not in the sense you're thinking. I will say a few things that look like objective truth, but they're going to be said through the lens of unreliable narrators. Even the pretty blunt &quot;clue&quot; in Secrets of the Covenants will probably create more questions than it answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:29:38-08:00","id":366712,"title":"","content":"Or in other words, we won't be told the facts any more clearly than the section in Blood And Smoke already does.<br /> <br /> That is all I wanted to know, so I'll make sure to avoid this gnawing riddle that I can't deal with. Thank you for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-11-2015, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T17:23:57-08:00","id":366743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=366712#post366712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or in other words, we won't be told the facts any more clearly than the section in Blood And Smoke already does.<br /> <br /> That is all I wanted to know, so I'll make sure to avoid this gnawing riddle that I can't deal with. Thank you for the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You'll get some things you may or may not take as facts. But I have no intention of making an out-of-character, stat-blocked declaration of exactly what the Nameless is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T17:45:57-08:00","id":366751,"title":"","content":"Same difference. And that wasn't what I was looking for anyways. If anything, I was looking for information in character that would actually offer us something concrete and objective to go on or clarify the nature of the Nameless and its machinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:53:44-08:00","id":370240,"title":"","content":"While I admit this is probably wrong, it might be interesting if the Nameless is somehow St.Longinus, The ghost of. I imagine his motivation would be that he's rather different than what the Sanctified claim, and is quite angry about what they say he was. While I'm not sure if the Owls can fuse with Ghosts, it's possible he's merged with a Strix that, as others have suggested, developed a hatred of European Kindred for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:22:00-08:00","id":370275,"title":"","content":"That would be interesting. It might be an interesting option to take if your story had some Lancea et Sanctum missionaries attempting to reassert the presence of the Lance in Montreal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T16:12:04-08:00","id":374538,"title":"","content":"Given how Rule 7 doesn't translate to human speech, I'm thinking Beast Speech-hiding the actual text in plain sight as bizarre pictographs. Which means Belial's Brood, most likely a covey of the Nameless in a relatively blatant mood. Perhaps they figured out a way to consecrate the Cross to the Adversary and thus designate Montreal as a No-God Zone, then took the opportunity to make it Forsworn territory, which they aren't particularly interested in ruling beyond it serving as a safe spot and to grow potential recruits given how horrible Unlearned existence is there. The reason why rule-breaking is so easily caught is that there are multiple Kindred on patrol as the Nameless at any given time, and violators quickly get ambushed and dogpiled by the entire membership of the Brood there. Of course, given how the Nameless are a <i>pnuema </i>faction, their membership can convincingly imitate humans while on said patrol...<br /> <br /> Said rule 7 is probably along the lines of &quot;If you can read this, you are authorized to violate the rules if you're smart about it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T17:53:59-08:00","id":374609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=374538#post374538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Rule 7 doesn't translate to human speech, I'm thinking Beast Speech-hiding the actual text in plain sight as bizarre pictographs. Which means Belial's Brood, most likely a covey of the Nameless in a relatively blatant mood. Perhaps they figured out a way to consecrate the Cross to the Adversary and thus designate Montreal as a No-God Zone, then took the opportunity to make it Forsworn territory, which they aren't particularly interested in ruling beyond it serving as a safe spot and to grow potential recruits given how horrible Unlearned existence is there. The reason why rule-breaking is so easily caught is that there are multiple Kindred on patrol as the Nameless at any given time, and violators quickly get ambushed and dogpiled by the entire membership of the Brood there. Of course, given how the Nameless are a <i>pnuema </i>faction, their membership can convincingly imitate humans while on said patrol...<br /> <br /> Said rule 7 is probably along the lines of &quot;If you can read this, you are authorized to violate the rules if you're smart about it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brood would have to mean something completely different than what we're used to. Which is not out of the question. <br /> <br /> And yeah. Didn't really address it, but Rule 7 should exist in plain sight. But not in actual text. It's the kind of law that needs to exist, even if nobody truly understands it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> DjNHn2fNLi3uWVJk+1dck4Wn6o7eq0OiVU8hMTEhBAO/O8bYi2HmFGqkfd/vITM5ITeHlc2/NzNqBAIhMTAhnnYXBJA+bB8p2Z99OK1+A3sPsUYEwRz9KdNwny E5Idsy7DSjLkdJIwM31tchMCFwzqWYOCWq<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T18:18:27-08:00","id":374642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=374609#post374609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DjNHn2fNLi3uWVJk+1dck4Wn6o7eq0OiVU8hMTEhBAO/O8bYi2HmFGqkfd/vITM5ITeHlc2/NzNqBAIhMTAhnnYXBJA+bB8p2Z99OK1+A3sPsUYEwRz9KdNwny E5Idsy7DSjLkdJIwM31tchMCFwzqWYOCWq</div> </div> </div> </div> Doesn't match any cypher I've put it through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T19:44:29-08:00","id":374699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=374609#post374609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Brood would have to mean something completely different than what we're used to. Which is not out of the question.<br /> <br /> And yeah. Didn't really address it, but Rule 7 should exist in plain sight. But not in actual text. It's the kind of law that needs to exist, even if nobody truly understands it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>that made me think while shaving right now. All of the rules have the same punishment- death. That is, if someone where to violate rule 7, he should have got killed. Yet, all the deaths we know about which were made by the Nameless come from following the known, 6 rules. That means one of the following:<br /> <br /> 1) No vampire violate rule 7 because it is an integral part of being a vampire<br /> 2) rule 7 is an integral part of the other rules, so violation them is like violating it- so any death made by the Nameless is also because the individual broke law 7.<br /> <br /> In each of those cases, there is no need to write down law 7, because the vampires would instinctively follow it, making it &quot;hidden in plain sight&quot;. Maybe it should be something like &quot;Fear the Nameless&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T11:06:12-08:00","id":377382,"title":"","content":"I should think the most obvious unstated rule from the Nameless is simply &quot;Don't name the Nameless&quot;. It seems entirely possible it is one of those things that is obvious to many of the characters in the city, they just don't name it because, well...yeah, that'll get you killed.<br /> <br /> Especially because of the whole &quot;Most importantly, Ventrue who speak with representatives of the Tsihstekeri line simply stop fearing the Nameless. None have said what they\u2019re told, but they become noticeably more afraid of something else entirely.&quot; thing. The question seems less &quot;what is the Nameless?&quot;, and more &quot;What are the Nameless' rules designed to protect Kindred from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:21:04-07:00","id":922154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=78249#post78249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The seventh rule doesn't translate to text.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinda renders discussion of Rule 7 moot, doesn't it? If it doesn't translate into text, nothing we post here is going to be it.<br /> <br /> Also, did anyone ever figure out what that weird string of characters was about?<br /> <br /> DjNHn2fNLi3uWVJk+1dck4Wn6o7eq0OiVU8hMTEhBAO/O8bYi2HmFGqkfd/vITM5ITeHlc2/NzNqBAIhMTAhnnYXBJA+bB8p2Z99OK1+A3sPsUYEwRz9KdNwny E5Idsy7DSjLkdJIwM31tchMCFwzqWYOCWq","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:05:19-07:00","id":922390,"title":"","content":"I always figured it was a particularly ancient and powerful Strix, possibly one that is possessing a vampire who is also particularly ancient and power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T05:22:18-07:00","id":922551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=922154#post922154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda renders discussion of Rule 7 moot, doesn't it? If it doesn't translate into text, nothing we post here is going to be it.<br /> <br /> Also, did anyone ever figure out what that weird string of characters was about?<br /> <br /> DjNHn2fNLi3uWVJk+1dck4Wn6o7eq0OiVU8hMTEhBAO/O8bYi2HmFGqkfd/vITM5ITeHlc2/NzNqBAIhMTAhnnYXBJA+bB8p2Z99OK1+A3sPsUYEwRz9KdNwny E5Idsy7DSjLkdJIwM31tchMCFwzqWYOCWq</div> </div> </div> </div> As the person who made the original comment about the seventh rule, let me post my thoughts - it was originally nothing more than a joking reference to the covenant VII. The original write up has six rules, listed with roman numerals. So, I immediately thought about VII as a result. Nothing more than a guess.<br /> <br /> Could be a clue, could be nothing more than Machine joking back. My thought was that the Namless is an example city where the VII were in power - as in, Ruled by VII. Certainly, I think that VII has the possibility of breaking Theban and effectively hunting down other vampires like the Nameless is. Sure, they're not leaving behind the big VII like usual, but its lack seemed just as suspicious and telling to me. VII now has the possibility of being tied to the God-Machine, so that could be a whole thing as well, explaining the religious references as well.<br /> <br /> As for the string for characters, it could just be gibberish instead of a cypher - how &quot;rule 7&quot; would look if translated to text. <br /> <br /> Honestly, its still nothing more than a half-baked theory. There's something about &quot;divine&quot; magic and crosses that need to be avoided for some reason. There's something about the Rue Saint Paul that I don't understand that either. Why only 4 vampires? That's about the standard party size, but that means that a group of PCs can't meet with even lone NPC vamps when together, making me wonder if there's more behind that number (more god-machine references come to mind, but it could just be me reaching).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T08:29:28-07:00","id":922644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=922551#post922551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, its still nothing more than a half-baked theory. There's something about &quot;divine&quot; magic and crosses that need to be avoided for some reason. There's something about the Rue Saint Paul that I don't understand that either. Why only 4 vampires? That's about the standard party size, but that means that a group of PCs can't meet with even lone NPC vamps when together, making me wonder if there's more behind that number (more god-machine references come to mind, but it could just be me reaching).</div> </div> </div> </div>In a meta sense, I saw it as an example setting geared towards Chronicles where there were only one or two PCs. <br /> <br /> In a narrative sense, maybe it's because there's a prophecy: only through the efforts of a coterie of five, containing a member of each clan, can the Nameless be defeated. To prevent this, the Nameless killed off any gathering of five or more, and set the limit at four, just one shy of fulfilling the prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:32:54-07:00","id":922852,"title":"","content":"Can I just say that Montreal was the highlight of VtR 2e for me and of all the 2e books so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:05:40-07:00","id":922866,"title":"","content":"A cult of Strix (It isn't just one Strix which is why the sizes vary in witness reports) working to maintain Infrastructure for the God-Machine (with an Angel manipulating the Strix as the cult leader) with the Cross acting as a Lynchpin for a ritual keeping Thesban sorcery from working. The God-Machine is channeling the potential death-tainted mystical power of self-loathing faith to its goals elsewhere, possibly stirring up zealots and martyrs to commit atrocities which power even greater gears fueled by human suffering and death, and to wind tight the mainspring of western paranoia, oppressive government in the name of safety against terrorism, and automation of military drone technology to set off the alarm-clock of Armageddon. Tick-tock tick-tock.<br /> <br /> The Strix go along because the Angel has persuaded them that it is an evolved form of them that has become a death-god, and they are working towards a goal that'll all eventually make them death gods too (which is a lie, but convinces them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:14:32-07:00","id":922870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=922866#post922866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cult of Strix (It isn't just one Strix which is why the sizes vary in witness reports) working to maintain Infrastructure for the God-Machine (with an Angel manipulating the Strix as the cult leader) with the Cross acting as a Lynchpin for a ritual keeping Thesban sorcery from working.<br /> <br /> The Strix go along because the Angel has persuaded them that it is an evolved form of them that has become a death-god, and they are working towards a goal that'll all eventually make them death gods too (which is a lie, but convinces them).</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this, please. Ye gods, that's brilliant. It answers the question of the &quot;greater threat&quot; that the Native Ventrue know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T12:44:14-07:00","id":923424,"title":"","content":"My three drops to this information creek (and i give it like this because of the mood in which the text has gotten me, sorry for the mysteriousness):<br /> <br /> 1. Paul de Chomedey.<br /> 2. The Rules are the Rules. The Carthian Movement has already won.<br /> 3. Ancient blood is blue blood.<br /> <br /> (Two more considerations: 1 - since the rules settlement the trespassers don't die; they <u><i>vanish</i></u>. 2 - Only the Carthians have <u><i>really</i></u> seen the Nameless)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:59:44-07:00","id":923685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_contai