s=\"message\">I ran that name through the almighty Wikipedia, and this little tidbit came out: he was the one who erected the Mount Royal Cross.<br /> <br /> ... Oh! ...Oh. ... Oh my.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And you can keep digging about him in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rue_Saint-Paul_(Montreal)\" target=\"_blank\">Rue Saint-Paul</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:23:59-07:00","id":924520,"title":"","content":"wait... Paul de Chomedey erected the Cross as a tribute to Virgin Mary for surviving a flood- does it mean that now, that the Cross is compromised by the Nameless, the flood is coming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:32:50-07:00","id":924620,"title":"","content":"I finally read the section and my first thought was an Eshmaki Tyrant Beast. Not exactly vampire tied and probably just cause I've been reading Beast lately but still what my immediate thought of the Nameless is.<br /> <br /> What happens if a Strix uses Synthesis on a Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:05:23-07:00","id":924634,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn Beasts had some 'no meddling with our soul' natural ability but with a quick glance I can't find it.<br /> <br /> Really all you would get is a better Beast that would likely strike off to rampant or incarnate inheritance pretty fast. Like a vampire without its natural weaknesses, but with the glutted hindrances of overfeeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:27:30-07:00","id":924750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=924520#post924520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait... Paul de Chomedey erected the Cross as a tribute to Virgin Mary for surviving a flood- does it mean that now, that the Cross is compromised by the Nameless, the flood is coming?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to favor the theory that not only has the Nameless compromised the Cross, he's Paul de freakin' Chomeday himself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:05:43-07:00","id":925107,"title":"","content":"My theory is that the Nameless calls itself so because its True Name - quite a big deal in egyptian mysticism, as much as ones <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egyptian_concept_of_the_soul\" target=\"_blank\">Ba and a number of other as</a>p<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egyptian_concept_of_the_soul\" target=\"_blank\">ects</a> - was lost somewhere in time and this is in some way tied to the LS<i>'</i> theft and bastardization of what would become Theban Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:12:55-07:00","id":925114,"title":"","content":"The Nameless doesn't seem to call itself that. The Carthians were attempting a takeover and a 'mysterious figure' wiped them out single-handedly and took the sole survivors eyes before giving her the six laws. She called him 'The Nameless.'<br /> <br /> There's an example Prince that basically acts like the Nameless in Danse Macabre, called the Phantom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-02-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:13:38-07:00","id":925116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=925107#post925107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory is that the Nameless calls itself so because its True Name - quite a big deal in egyptian mysticism, as much as ones <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egyptian_concept_of_the_soul&amp;quot;]Ba</a> and a number of other as[/URL]p<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egyptian_concept_of_the_soul&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">ects</a> - was lost somewhere in time and this is in some way tied to the LS<i>'</i> theft and bastardization of what would become Theban Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>How'd an Egyptian spirit get to Montreal long enough ago to befriend the native undead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:20:20-07:00","id":925121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=925116#post925116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How'd an Egyptian spirit get to Montreal long enough ago to befriend the native undead?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Chicago book, Upuaut, the Opener of the Way, comes to Chicago simply because it felt a call. It opens a way at a temple that happens to have some Egyptian artifacts, which I'm sure there's more than a few of in Montreal. At a certain point very powerful spirits aren't limited at all by geography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:03:55-07:00","id":925141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=922866#post922866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cult of Strix (It isn't just one Strix which is why the sizes vary in witness reports) working to maintain Infrastructure for the God-Machine (with an Angel manipulating the Strix as the cult leader) with the Cross acting as a Lynchpin for a ritual keeping Thesban sorcery from working. The God-Machine is channeling the potential death-tainted mystical power of self-loathing faith to its goals elsewhere, possibly stirring up zealots and martyrs to commit atrocities which power even greater gears fueled by human suffering and death, and to wind tight the mainspring of western paranoia, oppressive government in the name of safety against terrorism, and automation of military drone technology to set off the alarm-clock of Armageddon. Tick-tock tick-tock.<br /> <br /> The Strix go along because the Angel has persuaded them that it is an evolved form of them that has become a death-god, and they are working towards a goal that'll all eventually make them death gods too (which is a lie, but convinces them).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is so insanely meta-plot-ish. Loving it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:44:47-08:00","id":1016777,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants touched on Montreal and the Nameless in the Ordo Dravul section, FYI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank"